  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Monique, I checked the delivery records for all four orders. Two were late enough for compensation, so I've added **$30 in account credit** to your account. The other two don't qualify. Here's each one:\n\n**#6501 \u2013 Saffron Lane (tonight): $25 credit added**\nIt was promised for 6:00 PM and handed to you at 6:52 PM, 52 minutes late. For deliveries 45 or more minutes late, the credit is 20% of the subtotal, up to $25 for Plus orders. 20% of your $128 subtotal is $25.60, so you got the $25 maximum.\n\n**#6502 \u2013 Pho Real (Thursday): $5 credit added**\nIt was promised for 7:15 PM and handed to you at 7:45 PM, 30 minutes late. For a Plus order 16 to 44 minutes late, the credit is $5.\n\n**#6503 \u2013 Taqueria Luz (Tuesday): no credit**\nAt 5:50 PM we sent you a push notification moving the arrival time to 7:00 PM because of a courier shortage. That was more than 30 minutes before the original 6:30 PM time, so 7:00 PM became the promised time. The order arrived at 7:12 PM, 12 minutes after that. An order counts as late only if it arrives more than 15 minutes after the promised time.\n\n**#6504 \u2013 Burger Barn (last Friday, Oct 16): no credit**\nThis one was late: it was promised for 7:00 PM and arrived at 8:00 PM. However, late compensation can only be requested up to 7 days after delivery, and that window closed at 8:00 PM yesterday (Oct 23). I'm sorry I can't add credit for it.\n\nYour account credit is now **$30.00**, and it will be applied to your future orders. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks for checking. I'm not happy about #6503 and #6504 though. For #6503 I never got a notification about a move to 7:00, and I was waiting on that order from 6:30 on. For #6504 I know it was an hour late. Why did the window close before I found out? Can you tell me why those two don't count?\n\nThere's something else too. Thursday's #6502 from Pho Real was missing the summer rolls. I paid for them and they weren't in the bag."
  },
