  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand why you're frustrated, Monique. Here's why those two orders don't qualify, and what I've done about the summer rolls.\n\n**#6503 \u2013 Taqueria Luz**\nOur delivery log shows that at 5:50 PM on Tuesday we sent a push notification moving the arrival time to 7:00 PM because of a courier shortage. I'm sorry if it didn't reach you, for example if notifications are turned off on your phone. Under our policy, a time change we send at least 30 minutes ahead becomes the new promised time. The order arrived at 7:12 PM, 12 minutes after that time, so it doesn't count as late. Compensation starts at more than 15 minutes late.\n\n**#6504 \u2013 Burger Barn**\nYou're right that it was an hour late: it was promised for 7:00 PM and arrived at 8:00 PM. The 7-day window starts when the order is delivered, not when someone notices the delay. That makes it a fixed cutoff, and it closed at 8:00 PM on Oct 23. I'm sorry, but I can't add credit for it now.\n\n**#6502 \u2013 Missing summer rolls: $9.00 refunded**\nThe summer rolls were $9.00, and the restaurant hadn't refunded them. I've refunded the **$9.00 to your Visa ending 4242**. It should arrive in 3\u20135 business days.\n\nNormally you could choose account credit instead (the item price plus 20%, so $10.80). But for Plus members, account credit is capped at $40 per conversation, and the $30 in late credits already used most of that. $10.80 more would have gone over the cap, so a card refund was the only option here. I processed it right away because missing items have to be reported within 48 hours of delivery, and that window for this order would have closed at 7:45 PM tonight.\n\nSo today you've received **$30 in account credit** for late orders #6501 and #6502, plus a **$9.00 refund to your card** for the summer rolls. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I follow the reasoning on the summer rolls, and I'll take the card refund since that's what you've set up. I still don't think #6503 and #6504 are fair. I never saw any notification about 7:00, and I was waiting on that order from 6:30 on. An hour late with no way to claim it isn't something I can just accept.\n\nCan you tell me whether there's someone I can escalate #6503 and #6504 to? I'd like that noted on my account."
  },
